{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# ML-04 — Data Contract and a Small Feature Frame\n\nThis notebook documents my lane's slice of the warehouse, proves three facts about a mid-panel month (month=2026-03), builds five small features, and demonstrates the common leakage trap (on purpose) then removes it.\n\nNotes: this notebook queries the gated Hugging Face warehouse. Follow the instructions in the first code cell to set `HF_TOKEN` as an environment variable or Colab secret before running."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1) The contract (plain words — five short answers)\n\n1. What one row means for my lane:\n\nOne row = one pseudonymized content item for one client aggregated to a calendar-month summary (a content×client×month row). This row summarizes that month's observed search+engagement signals for the content as seen by that client.\n\n2. Which table(s) I'll use:\n\nPrimary: `fact_content_daily_performance` (aggregate into month). Joins to `dim_content` for stable content metadata.\n\n3. Time window I'll use for prototyping:\n\nA mid-panel month: month = `2026-03` (features built from that month). The final month (June 2026) will be reserved as the sealed test window.\n\n4. What I'd predict or rank (label / proxy):\n\nRank pages by the probability they will *decline* in impressions in the next 30 days after the feature month (a future-window decline label). For the starter checks we show supply-side facts; the full label requires forward-window aggregation.\n\n5. One thing I deliberately exclude:\n\nI will exclude any productscore or derived decision flags (e.g., `health_score`, `priority_score`) and I will never use `trend_direction` or `trend_pct` as features — they are label-derived and leak the answer."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Setup cell: set HF_TOKEN before running (Colab: use os.environ['HF_TOKEN'] or Colab secrets).\n",
    "# This notebook queries the Hugging Face dataset 'FlyRank/internship-warehouse'.\n",
    "# You MUST provide a valid HF_TOKEN in your environment BEFORE running these cells.\n",
    "# Example in a local shell: export HF_TOKEN=hf_...\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "hf_token = os.environ.get('HF_TOKEN')\n",
    "if not hf_token:\n",
    "    print('WARNING: HF_TOKEN not found in environment. Set HF_TOKEN and re-run the notebook to query the gated warehouse.')\n",
    "\n",
    "# We'll use the huggingface datasets library + duckdb for SQL-style queries on the parquet tables.\n",
    "from datasets import load_dataset\n",
    "import duckdb\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE: these load_dataset calls will only succeed when HF_TOKEN is set and the dataset access was requested/approved.\n",
    "# They are written defensively so you can run the notebook once you have a token.\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_table(table_name):\n",
    "    # load as a streaming dataset to avoid downloading everything locally\n",
    "    print(f'Attempting to load table: {table_name}')\n",
    "    ds = load_dataset('FlyRank/internship-warehouse', name=table_name, use_auth_token=hf_token, streaming=True)\n",
    "    return ds\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example usage (uncomment to run when HF_TOKEN is set):\n",
    "# ds_daily = load_table('fact_content_daily_performance')\n",
    "# ds_dim = load_table('dim_content')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Setup complete — set HF_TOKEN and run the queries below.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2) Prove three facts with three small queries (month = 2026-03)\n\nWe will run three verification queries on `fact_content_daily_performance` for `month = '2026-03'`. The checks: (A) grain probe: one row per (report_date, client_hash_id, content_hash_id) — there should be no duplicates; (B) row count and date span for that month; (C) availability: rows with GA4 data available (use `ga4_data_available IS TRUE`) and GSC data available checks.\n\nRun the cells below once your HF_TOKEN is in place. The queries use DuckDB to query the streamed dataset."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Query implementation using duckdb and the Hugging Face dataset streaming iterator.\n",
    "# For performance we will download only the month partition's parquet files if available via the dataset's files list.\n",
    "\n",
    "import duckdb\n",
    "from datasets import get_dataset_config_names, load_dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "month = '2026-03'  # mid-panel month for checks\n",
    "\n",
    "if hf_token:\n",
    "    # load the dataset metadata (not streaming) to find files — this may still require auth.\n",
    "    print('Loading dataset config names (may require auth)...')\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        configs = get_dataset_config_names('FlyRank/internship-warehouse')\n",
    "        print('Available table configs (example):', configs[:10])\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print('Could not list configs — proceeding to attempt loading the daily fact streaming table directly.', e)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Attempt a streaming load of the fact table and materialize the month partition into a small parquet temp table for duckdb.\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        ds = load_dataset('FlyRank/internship-warehouse', name='fact_content_daily_performance', use_auth_token=hf_token, streaming=True)\n",
    "        print('Streaming dataset loaded — filtering for month=', month)\n",
    "        # Convert the filtered streaming iterator into a pandas DataFrame (careful: may be large; here we limit)\n",
    "        it = ds.filter(lambda r: r.get('month') == month)\n",
    "        # materialize a sample to work with in these checks (we will take up to 200000 rows to keep memory reasonable)\n",
    "        df_month = pd.DataFrame(it.take(200000))\n",
    "        print('Materialized rows (sample cap 200k):', len(df_month))\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print('Could not stream or materialize the fact table — check HF_TOKEN and dataset access:', e)\n",
    "        df_month = pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Now run the three checks if df_month has rows\n",
    "    if len(df_month):\n",
    "        # A) Grain probe: any duplicates on the daily grain?\n",
    "        dup = df_month.duplicated(subset=['report_date','client_hash_id','content_hash_id']).sum()\n",
    "        print('A) Duplicate rows at (report_date, client, content):', dup)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # B) Row count and date span\n",
    "        print('B) Row count (sample):', len(df_month))\n",
    "        print('   Date span (min/max report_date):', df_month['report_date'].min(), df_month['report_date'].max())\n",
    "\n",
    "        # C) Availability check: GA4 / GSC flags (IS TRUE style)\n",
    "        # The dataset uses boolean-like flags; we check them explicitly for True.\n",
    "        ga4_true = (df_month['ga4_data_available'] == True).sum()\n",
    "        gsc_true = (df_month['gsc_data_available'] == True).sum()\n",
    "        print('C) ga4_data_available IS TRUE rows (sample):', int(ga4_true))\n",
    "        print('   gsc_data_available IS TRUE rows (sample):', int(gsc_true))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('No rows materialized for month — ensure HF_TOKEN and dataset access are correct.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('HF_TOKEN not set — cannot query the gated warehouse from here. Please set HF_TOKEN and re-run.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3) Build five features (small feature frame) — using month = 2026-03\n\nBelow we build a small per-content×client feature frame aggregated over the month partition. Each feature has one line explaining why it is knowable at decision time. These are intentionally simple and explainable."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Build five features on the materialized df_month (if available). Run after the previous cell.\n",
    "if 'df_month' in globals() and len(df_month):\n",
    "    # aggregate to content × client level for the month\n",
    "    group_cols = ['client_hash_id','content_hash_id']\n",
    "    agg = df_month.groupby(group_cols).agg(\n",
    "        impressions_month = ('impressions','sum'),\n",
    "        clicks_month = ('clicks','sum'),\n",
    "        avg_position = ('gsc_avg_position','mean'),\n",
    "        ai_sessions_month = ('sessions_ai','sum'),\n",
    "        days_with_impr = ('impressions','apply', lambda s: (s>0).sum())\n",
    "    ).reset_index()\n",
    "    # compute derived CTR (watch for zero impressions)\n",
    "    agg['ctr_month'] = agg['clicks_month'] / agg['impressions_month'] * 100\n",
    "    display_cols = ['client_hash_id','content_hash_id','impressions_month','clicks_month','ctr_month','avg_position','ai_sessions_month','days_with_impr']\n",
    "    print('Feature frame sample:')\n",
    "    display(agg[display_cols].head(8))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Feature availability lines (plain English)\n",
    "    feature_lines = [\n",
    "        ("impressions_month", "Sum of impressions in month 2026-03 — knowable at decision time because GSC impressions for the month are a historical signal already recorded by the end of the month."),\n",
    "        ("ctr_month", "Clicks / impressions ×100 for month — knowable because clicks and impressions are recorded in the same month; compute safely when impressions > 0."),\n",
    "        ("avg_position", "Mean GSC position for the month (ignore zeros meaning 'no_data') — knowable as an aggregated historic signal."),\n",
    "        ("ai_sessions_month", "Sum of AI-referred sessions in the month — knowable from GA4/AI logs recorded for the month; note this signal is sparse.") ,\n",
    "        ("days_with_impr", "Count of days in the month with >=1 impression — knowable from daily facts and useful to filter noise."),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    print('\nFeature availability notes:')\n",
    "    for name, note in feature_lines:\n",
    "        print('-', name + ':', note)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No df_month materialized — set HF_TOKEN and re-run the verification step to build the sample for the leakage demo.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4) The trap (leakage experiment) — one label-derived column on purpose\n\nWe will add a column that is derived from the target window or from trend buckets (for example `trend_pct` or `trend_direction`) and show how using it as a feature makes a quick model appear to do extremely well. Then we remove it and keep the honest metric. This demonstrates why derived trend fields that are computed using the same windows that define the label are leakage.\n\nDo this only on a small materialized sample (we do not retrain on the full warehouse here). The code below:\n- constructs `trend_pct` as (impressions_last_30d - impressions_prev_30d) / impressions_prev_30d × 100 if the per-row columns exist;\n- trains a quick logistic regression that uses only `trend_pct` to predict `is_declining_label` (this will be near-perfect because the label is derived from trend fields), prints AUC;\n- then removes the column and trains the same model on honest features and prints AUC for comparison.\n\nRun the cell below only after the month materialization and after you understand the warnings above."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Leakage experiment — requires that df_month contains the per-row trend columns used in the starter snapshot.\n",
    "if 'df_month' in globals() and len(df_month):\n",
    "    # Prepare a small modeling frame: aggregate the last-30/prev-30 columns if present at the row level\n",
    "    cols_needed = ['content_hash_id','client_hash_id','impressions_last_30d','impressions_prev_30d','trend_pct','trend_direction','is_declining_label']\n",
    "    missing = [c for c in cols_needed if c not in df_month.columns]\n",
    "    if missing:\n",
    "        print('Missing columns for the leakage demo:', missing)\n",
    "        print('If impressions_last_30d / impressions_prev_30d / trend_* columns are missing in the daily fact, you may need to join dim_content or use the starter CSV for this demo instead.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # collapse to content×client (take ANY_VALUE semantics where appropriate)\n",
    "        demo = df_month.groupby(['client_hash_id','content_hash_id']).agg({\n",
    "            'impressions_last_30d':'sum',\n",
    "            'impressions_prev_30d':'sum',\n",
    "            'trend_pct':'mean',\n",
    "            'is_declining_label':'max'\n",
    "        }).reset_index()\n",
    "        # compute a simple trend_pct if not present robustly\n",
    "        demo['trend_pct_calc'] = (demo['impressions_last_30d'] - demo['impressions_prev_30d']) / (demo['impressions_prev_30d'].replace(0, pd.NA)) * 100\n",
    "        demo['trend_pct_calc'] = demo['trend_pct_calc'].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "        # quick model: predict is_declining_label from trend_pct_calc (leaky) vs honest features (impressions_month, ctr_month) if available\n",
    "        from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "        from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n",
    "        \n",
    "        X_leak = demo[['trend_pct_calc']].fillna(0)\n",
    "        y = demo['is_declining_label'].astype(int)\n",
    "        if len(y.unique()) < 2:\n",
    "            print('Not enough class variety for AUC demo in the materialized sample.')\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            mdl = LogisticRegression(max_iter=200)\n",
    "            mdl.fit(X_leak, y)\n",
    "            preds = mdl.predict_proba(X_leak)[:,1]\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                auc_leak = roc_auc_score(y, preds)\n",
    "                print('AUC using leaky trend_pct_calc as the only feature:', auc_leak)\n",
    "            except Exception as e:\n",
    "                print('Could not compute AUC (maybe constant labels):', e)\n",
    "            # Now honest features: impressions_last_30d and impressions_prev_30d ratio removed? we'll use impressions as proxy features\n",
    "            X_honest = demo[['impressions_last_30d','impressions_prev_30d']].fillna(0)\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                mdl2 = LogisticRegression(max_iter=200)\n",
    "                mdl2.fit(X_honest, y)\n",
    "                preds2 = mdl2.predict_proba(X_honest)[:,1]\n",
    "                auc_honest = roc_auc_score(y, preds2)\n",
    "                print('AUC using honest impression features:', auc_honest)\n",
    "            except Exception as e:\n",
    "                print('Could not fit honest model (maybe constant features):', e)\n",
    "            print('\nLeakage lesson: trend-derived fields are the label source; they produce optimistic scores if reused as features. Remove them from training data.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('df_month not materialized — run the verification cell first with HF_TOKEN set to build the sample for the leakage demo.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5) Limitation and self-check\n\nLimitation: the warehouse is an unbalanced panel — per-client history depth varies, and some clients have little or no GA4 data. This means global thresholds can be misleading; prefer per-client windows and client-holdout validation.\n\nSelf-check before you submit:\n- [ ] The five contract answers are filled (above).\n- [ ] I ran the three verification queries on month=2026-03 and inspected outputs.\n- [ ] I built the five-feature frame and documented when each feature is available.\n- [ ] I ran the leakage experiment, observed the jump, then removed the leaky column before any honest model training.\n- [ ] I recorded the named limitation clearly.\n\nWhen ready, commit and submit: work/notebooks/w03_data_contract.ipynb"
  }
 ],
